{
  "title": "Ingredient catalog step 3: LLM-resolve unrecognized ingredient names into a persistent shared resolution table",
  "description": "Even after step 2, new recipes will bring names the committed catalog doesn't know. \
Resolve those with an LLM once per distinct name, persist the answer, and resolve at read time from catalog + table.\n\
\n\
Design:\n\
- Resolution stays at read time: resolve(item) checks the committed catalog/aliases, then a shared DB table (e.g. ingredient_resolutions: normalized_name unique, catalog_id or null for not-a-food, model, created_at). \
It's a local indexed lookup with no TTL, so it's fast and consistent, and catalog improvements apply to every recipe immediately with no backfill. \
Nothing is stored on the recipe's ingredients. \
Diesel DSL, no raw SQL.\n\
- Reads never call the LLM. \
The table is populated at write time: after any ingest or save (scrape, paste/text import, photo import, Paprika import, manual edit), collect the recipe's names that miss both catalog and table and resolve them in one batched LLM call. \
The call picks from candidate catalog ids shortlisted by lexical similarity to keep the prompt small, or answers not-a-food/unknown; it may only choose existing ids and never invents nutrition numbers. \
A name hit concurrently by two saves resolves once (unique constraint).\n\
- A read that hits a name not yet in the table (e.g. recipes imported before this ships, or a failed resolution) reports it as unknown. \
A one-off make target warms the table for all existing recipes.\n\
- Unknown stays unknown (the UI in p1-calorie-estimate-ux handles it); never treat an unresolved line as zero calories.\n\
- Harvest: a make target exports the table so the step 2 process can review entries and promote good ones into the committed catalog, keeping the runtime table a shrinking fallback.\n\
- For the paste flow, the resolution can be folded into the extraction call itself; see p2-text-import-structured-ingredients.\n\
\n\
Needs end-to-end tests with the mock OpenRouter fixture server (make mock-openrouter).",
